      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DAPPER CHAP (3) flew the lids from out wide with an impressive turn of foot, going on to clock 29.82 when a nose winner over 515m at Sandown last time. Strong form has emerged from his last run. Can make it back-to-back wins. HOKKAIDO EXPRESS (4) turned in a modest effort most recently when sixth at Geelong over 400m behind Coolabah Station (22.88) in a Grade 4/5. Has performed well from this box with a win and two minor placings to his name from four starts. Should play a prominent role. JULY SHE LIED (2) looks close to another win after finishing second last time (22.60) at Ballarat. Solid winning record at this trip. Can measure up. STERLING INN (1) is always hard to beat when drawn in this box.",
